CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM
---------------------

Per Apache License 2.0 section 4(b), the following states the changes made to
the original work. This is a summary; see the git history for detail.

Added:

  * gateway/ - agentic-imapd, an IMAP and SMTP submission server in Go. This
    is independent work, not derived from the upstream project. It is a
    separate Go module with its own LICENSE and NOTICE.
  * Raw RFC 5322 message retention in R2 for inbound and outbound mail, so
    the original bytes can be served rather than a reconstruction.
  * Per-mailbox app passwords (workers/lib/credentials.ts) and a rate limiter
    for them (workers/durableObject/authRateLimit.ts).
  * An HTTP API for mail clients under /api/imap/v1
    (workers/routes/imap-api.ts): authentication, folder and message listing,
    raw message retrieval, flag writes, copy, move, expunge, append, and SMTP
    submission.
  * A test suite. The upstream project had no test framework.
  * Continuous integration.

Modified:

  * workers/durableObject/ - schema migration adding IMAP identity (per-folder
    UIDs, UIDVALIDITY), IMAP flags, message size and raw-object references,
    plus the read and write methods those endpoints require. Reference-counted
    R2 cleanup on delete.
  * workers/index.ts - inbound mail now stores the raw message; the delete
    path purges R2 objects it previously leaked.
  * workers/lib/tools.ts, workers/routes/reply-forward.ts - outbound paths now
    store a raw copy of what was sent.
  * workers/app.ts - mounts the new API surface.
  * README.md - rewritten to describe this fork.

